{"skill":{"slug":"ffmpeg-cli","displayName":"FFmpeg CLI"},"version":{"version":"1.0.0","createdAt":1769579607401,"changelog":"Initial release: comprehensive video/audio processing with cut, merge, extract-audio, thumb, gif, convert, speed, watermark scripts","changelogSource":"user","license":null,"files":[{"path":"SKILL.md","size":2559,"sha256":"ef9ff1fb135c4919f688ae07cf9a3ba5a537ebd5e76f00edd3afad2e537a8a2d","contentType":"text/markdown"},{"path":"scripts/convert.sh","size":542,"sha256":"6e34e9616b48ec572611566ed8a2a5433f999286f7a66e095fb5feb1bdcc1292","contentType":"application/x-sh"},{"path":"scripts/cut.sh","size":760,"sha256":"1564c62adbf80688d94eecf2cba87198cbb27c37443967431d195019ddd116ec","contentType":"application/x-sh"},{"path":"scripts/extract-audio.sh","size":525,"sha256":"bec67bc0e3f61345295a6de972d96accdade2b24b92620a29f8df9116ae73d0c","contentType":"application/x-sh"},{"path":"scripts/gif.sh","size":819,"sha256":"6c0edd53350ef5ec7b0b6610af5679b964343ef227ed65a040e782b3b9399987","contentType":"application/x-sh"},{"path":"scripts/merge.sh","size":686,"sha256":"9f9d17ad100025f30fd6479ebeafd655f21c9f6274f25142699d0c14f4ef0217","contentType":"application/x-sh"},{"path":"scripts/speed.sh","size":1007,"sha256":"a196a9f756e6490e61afeec04954750a0193298369a2ce41fc40957de58d657c","contentType":"application/x-sh"},{"path":"scripts/thumb.sh","size":670,"sha256":"febe691943ffcfe8e7a17440bff734ebaa37a92308b7191be21a85f82b9a0e1c","contentType":"application/x-sh"},{"path":"scripts/watermark.sh","size":733,"sha256":"415843828e0387a55a2fbcc83669c724e82f5ec2e0ef74bea49413545387a9e0","contentType":"application/x-sh"},{"path":"skill-card.md","size":1758,"sha256":"616dae0cbaf5c151b7bf80ca3e800e8e6d484ef61956fd92fdadc1ab7095df2c","contentType":"text/markdown"}],"security":{"status":"suspicious","hasWarnings":true,"checkedAt":1789024824612,"model":null,"hasScanResult":true,"sha256hash":"8ba9d16a01dd8470ce65aa5846e2ea106af4054bc3bb020236abd2ed489e42bc","virustotalUrl":"https://www.virustotal.com/gui/file/8ba9d16a01dd8470ce65aa5846e2ea106af4054bc3bb020236abd2ed489e42bc","scanners":{"vt":{"status":"suspicious","verdict":"suspicious","normalizedStatus":"suspicious","analysis":"Type: OpenClaw Skill\nName: ffmpeg-cli\nVersion: 1.0.0\n\nThe `merge.sh` script is vulnerable to command injection. It constructs a temporary file (`TEMP_LIST`) from user-supplied arguments without sanitization and then uses `ffmpeg -f concat -safe 0 -i \"$TEMP_LIST\"`. The `-safe 0` option disables security checks for the concat demuxer, allowing `ffmpeg` to interpret `file 'pipe:...'` entries in the list as commands. A malicious actor providing crafted input (e.g., `file 'pipe:cat /etc/passwd'`) to the `merge.sh` script could achieve arbitrary command execution or data exfiltration, making this a significant risky capability.","source":"palm","checkedAt":1779160181575},"skillspector":{"status":"suspicious","normalizedStatus":"suspicious","score":18,"severity":"LOW","recommendation":"CAUTION","issueCount":2,"checkedAt":1789024824612},"llm":{"status":"suspicious","verdict":"suspicious","normalizedStatus":"suspicious","confidence":"high","summary":"This is a normal FFmpeg helper skill, but its scripts can overwrite files without confirmation and include unsafe input handling that users should review first.","dimensions":[{"detail":"The scripts run FFmpeg with the current user's local filesystem permissions, accept arbitrary input and output paths, and lack validation or containment around destructive overwrites and concat/filter expression inputs.","label":"Credentials","name":"environment_proportionality","rating":"concern"},{"detail":"The declared install path only requires FFmpeg via Homebrew; no post-install script, remote payload retrieval, or dependency confusion pattern was found in the artifact.","label":"Install Mechanism","name":"install_mechanism","rating":"ok"},{"detail":"The instructions do not warn that the scripts pass -y to FFmpeg and will replace an existing output path, and merge.sh builds an FFconcat control file from raw filenames while speed.sh accepts an unrestricted rate despite documenting a 0.5-2.0 range.","label":"Instruction Scope","name":"instruction_scope","rating":"concern"},{"detail":"No credential access, privilege escalation, shell profile modification, scheduled task, service, background worker, or cross-session persistence behavior was found.","label":"Persistence & Privilege","name":"persistence_privilege","rating":"ok"},{"detail":"The skill purpose, documentation, and scripts coherently focus on local FFmpeg video and audio processing; the concerns are implementation safety issues rather than hidden or unrelated capability.","label":"Purpose & Capability","name":"purpose_capability","rating":"note"}],"guidance":"Review this skill before installing if an agent may process untrusted filenames or choose output paths automatically. Use it only with deliberate output filenames, avoid overwriting valuable files, and avoid feeding it attacker-controlled media paths, playback rates, or watermark positions unless the scripts are hardened first.","findings":"[SQP-2] expected: Use of FFmpeg to write output files is expected for this media-processing skill, but the artifact confirms unconditional -y overwrites in multiple scripts, including the reported speed.sh and watermark.sh cases, without explicit user confirmation or documentation.\n[T09] unexpected: The merge.sh finding is supported by artifact evidence: raw filenames are written into an FFconcat control file and processed with -safe 0, which is an avoidable unsafe parsing pattern for untrusted filenames.\n[T09] unexpected: The speed.sh finding is supported by artifact evidence: RATE is passed into bc and FFmpeg filter expressions without syntax or range validation, despite the skill documentation presenting a bounded numeric interface.","agenticRiskFindings":null,"riskSummary":null,"model":null,"checkedAt":1789024824612}}}}}